@startuml class-integration-backend
' Class diagram: IntegrationBackend interface + concrete backends (DIP).
'
' Grounded in real source:
'   - src/integration/IntegrationBackend.h  (interface + BackendState enum)
'   - src/integration/IntegrationManager.h  (owns backends by interface)
'   - src/integration/TcpBackend.h
'   - src/integration/MqttClient.h  (also TelemetryPublisher/Subscriber)
'   - src/integration/HttpBackend.h
'   - src/integration/HttpTlsMaterial.h / HttpTlsOptions.h
'   - src/integration/modbus/ModbusBackend.h
'   - src/integration/opcua/OpcUaBackend.h
'   - src/integration/opcua/Open62541SecurityMaterial.h
'   - src/integration/opcua/OpcUaSecurityOptions.h / OpcUaSecurityReport.h
' Signatures copied verbatim from those headers.

title IntegrationBackend - interface + concretes (Dependency Inversion)

skinparam shadowing false
hide empty members

enum BackendState {
  Disconnected
  Connecting
  Connected
  Degraded
}

interface IntegrationBackend {
  +start() : void
  +stop() : void
  +isRunning() : bool
  +name() : string
  +connectionState() : BackendState
  +metricsSummary() : string
}
IntegrationBackend ..> BackendState

class IntegrationManager {
  +registerBackend(unique_ptr<IntegrationBackend>)
  +startAll()
  +stopAll() noexcept
  +allRunning() : bool
  +backends() : vector<unique_ptr<IntegrationBackend>>&
  +lastStartErrors() : vector<string>&
}
IntegrationManager o--> "*" IntegrationBackend : owns\n(treats uniformly, never downcasts)

class TcpBackend {
  name() = "TCP"
  +boundPort() : uint16_t
  +activeClients() : size_t
}
class MqttClient {
  name() = "MQTT" (3.1.1, QoS0)
  +publish(topic, payload)
  +subscribe(filter, cb)
}
class HttpBackend {
  name() = "HTTP" (read-only REST)
  +routePaths() : vector<string_view>
  +tlsEnabled() : bool
}

class HttpTlsOptions <<value>> {
  +certPath : string
  +keyPath : string
  +verifyPeer : bool
  +clientCaPath : string
}

class HttpTlsMaterial {
  +HttpTlsMaterial(HttpTlsOptions)
  +options() : const HttpTlsOptions&
  +verifiesPeer() : bool
}
class ModbusBackend {
  name() = "Modbus"
  composes client+map+bridge+pollLoop
}
class OpcUaBackend {
  name() = "OPC-UA"
  composes server + nodeMap
  metricsSummary() probes OpcUaSecurityReport
}

interface OpcUaSecurityReport {
  +securityModeName() : string_view
}

class Open62541Server {
  +start() / +stop() noexcept
  +boundPort() : uint16_t
  +securityModeName() : string_view
}

class OpcUaSecurityOptions <<value>> {
  +enabled : bool
  +certPath : string
  +privateKeyPath : string
  +trustListDir : string
  +configKeyPrefix : string
}

class Open62541SecurityMaterial {
  +Open62541SecurityMaterial(OpcUaSecurityOptions)
  +certificate() : const UA_ByteString&
  +privateKey() : const UA_ByteString&
  +trustList() : const UA_ByteString*
  +trustListSize() : size_t
}
class SerialBackend {
  name() = "Serial"
  boost::asio::serial_port async read loop
  feeds SerialFrameParser -> ReadingSink
}

interface TelemetryPublisher
interface TelemetrySubscriber

IntegrationBackend <|.. TcpBackend
IntegrationBackend <|.. MqttClient
IntegrationBackend <|.. HttpBackend
IntegrationBackend <|.. ModbusBackend
IntegrationBackend <|.. OpcUaBackend
IntegrationBackend <|.. SerialBackend

TelemetryPublisher  <|.. MqttClient
TelemetrySubscriber <|.. MqttClient

HttpBackend o--> "0..1" HttpTlsMaterial : proven at construction
HttpTlsMaterial *--> HttpTlsOptions : holds the paths it verified

OpcUaSecurityReport <|.. Open62541Server
OpcUaBackend o--> "1" Open62541Server : owns via OpcUaServer
OpcUaBackend ..> OpcUaSecurityReport : dynamic_cast probe\n(optional capability)
Open62541Server o--> "0..1" Open62541SecurityMaterial : proven in the constructor
Open62541SecurityMaterial *--> OpcUaSecurityOptions : holds the paths it loaded

note right of HttpTlsMaterial
  ADR-0030: the cert / key (/ client CA) are
  loaded and checked BEFORE any port is bound.
  A failure is a fatal core::TlsMaterialError,
  never a silent fallback to plaintext.
end note

note right of Open62541SecurityMaterial
  ADR-0031: DER material for Basic256Sha256
  SignAndEncrypt, loaded in the CONSTRUCTOR so a
  bad certificate throws before any UA_Server
  exists. Same fatal core::TlsMaterialError.
  The one opcua type that does NOT hide open62541:
  UA_ByteString is its whole public surface.
end note

note bottom of OpcUaSecurityReport
  ISP: OpcUaServer keeps itself to what a node map
  and a command sink need, so encryption gets its
  own interface. A server with no security story
  implements nothing extra, and MockOpcUaServer
  stays unchanged.
end note

note bottom of IntegrationManager
  DIP: the manager depends only on the
  IntegrationBackend abstraction. Adding a
  protocol = a new subclass; manager unchanged (O of SOLID).
end note

@enduml
